= Control Total Geography Pipeline =

This page documents the [https://github.com/psrc/control_total_geography control_total_geography] repository, which builds the '''control''' and '''control_hct''' spatial layers used as the geographic foundation for PSRC's control totals process. The pipeline also produces '''target''' and '''cities''' geography layers and flags parcels by transit-oriented development (TOD) category. It is configured via <code>settings.yaml</code> and executed as a series of ordered [https://pypyr.io/ pypyr] steps.

== Overview ==

The pipeline follows six phases:

# '''Data Loading''' — Load CSV crosswalks from the <code>data/</code> folder and pull geospatial feature classes from PSRC's ElmerGeo database into a local pipeline cache.
# '''Control Geography Creation''' — Union PSRC regional geography (jurisdictions/UGAs), military bases, tribal land, and natural resource areas into a single set of control area polygons, each with a unique <code>control_id</code>.
# '''Target & Cities Geography''' — Dissolve control areas up to target areas (for growth-target aggregation) and extract a separate cities layer with a parcel–city crosswalk.
# '''Parcel HCT/TOD Flagging''' — Flag every parcel as rural, urban center, and/or within a high-capacity-transit (HCT) stop buffer, then assign a TOD code and a <code>control_hct_id</code>.
# '''Control HCT Geography''' — Dissolve flagged parcel polygons by <code>control_id</code>/<code>control_hct_id</code> to build the <code>control_hct</code> layer (control areas split into HCT / non-HCT sub-areas).
# '''Output Export''' — Write the final geography layers and tables from the pipeline cache to a file geodatabase and CSV files.

