== Configuration ==

Key settings from <code>settings.yaml</code>:

{| class="wikitable"
! Setting !! Example Value !! Description
|-
| <code>data_dir</code> || <code>data</code> || Folder (relative to configs dir) containing input CSV crosswalks
|-
| <code>pipeline_dir</code> || <code>pipeline</code> || Folder where intermediate parquet tables are cached between steps
|-
| <code>output_dir</code> || <code>Q:/Projects/.../control_geographies</code> || Folder where the final geodatabase and CSVs are written
|-
| <code>control_areas_year</code> || 2026 || Year used to suffix output layer names (e.g. <code>control26</code>)
|-
| <code>nat_resource_sliver_buffer</code> || 500 || Buffer distance (feet) used to snap small sliver polygons back into natural resource areas
|-
| <code>jurisdictions_to_explode</code> || <code>[Renton PAA]</code> || Jurisdictions that must be split into multiple control areas rather than kept as one polygon
|-
| <code>jblm_uga_control_id</code> || 405 || Control ID for the JBLM (Joint Base Lewis-McChord) UGA, carved out before the military-base union
|-
| <code>tribal_areas_keep</code> || <code>{Tulalip Reservation: 210}</code> || Tribal areas to retain as their own control area, mapped to a control ID
|-
| <code>nat_resource_county_map</code> || <code>{'033': 301, ...}</code> || Maps county FIPS to the control ID used for that county's natural resource area
|-
| <code>hct_buffers</code> || <code>{brt: 1320, commuter_r: 2640, light_rail: 2640, ferry: 2640}</code> || Buffer distance (feet) around each HCT stop type used for parcel flagging
|-
| <code>ElmerGeo</code> || — || List of ElmerGeo/Elmer tables to pull, each with a <code>name</code>, <code>sql_table</code>, <code>columns</code>, and optional <code>id_col</code>
|-
| <code>data_tables</code> || — || List of local CSV crosswalks to load, each with a <code>name</code> and <code>file</code>
|-
| <code>output_geodatabase</code> || <code>control.gdb</code> || File geodatabase name for exported layers
|-
| <code>output_layers</code> || <code>[control, control_hct, target, cities]</code> || Geodataframe layers exported to the output geodatabase
|-
| <code>output_tables</code> || <code>[parcels_control_hct, parcels_cities]</code> || Tabular outputs exported to CSV
