== Key Concepts ==

=== Control Areas ===
The fundamental geographic unit for this pipeline. Each control area has a unique <code>control_id</code> and is built by unioning PSRC jurisdiction/UGA boundaries with military bases, tribal land, and natural resource areas so that every acre in the region is covered by exactly one control area.

=== Control HCT ===
A finer split of each control area into an HCT (high-capacity-transit-served) sub-area and a non-HCT sub-area, identified by <code>control_hct_id</code> = <code>control_id</code> + 1000. Built by dissolving parcel polygons according to each parcel's TOD flag.

=== Target Areas ===
Groups of one or more control areas, identified by <code>target_id</code>. This is the level at which county growth targets are assigned in the downstream control-totals process (see the [https://github.com/psrc/control_totals control_totals] repository).

=== Pipeline Cache ===
The <code>util.Pipeline</code> class provides a lightweight persistence layer: tables are saved as parquet files under <code>pipeline_dir</code>; geodataframes are saved the same way using geopandas' native GeoParquet support, which preserves the CRS in the file metadata so it round-trips correctly on read instead of being reassigned a default.

=== Jurisdictions to Explode ===
Some jurisdictions (e.g. Renton PAA) need to be split into more than one control area. These are pulled out of the regional layer, spatially joined to the prior year's control areas (<code>CONTROL18_DASHBOARD</code>) to inherit multiple <code>control_id</code>s, and dissolved back in.

=== Natural Resource Slivers ===
When natural resource/forest/park polygons are overlaid with county boundaries, small sliver polygons can result along the edges. The pipeline buffers the resource polygons by <code>nat_resource_sliver_buffer</code> feet and merges any unlabeled slivers whose representative point falls in that buffer back into the resource area, so they aren't left as separate tiny control areas.

